WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.780
Let the battle begin.

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:05.939
With the arrival of director Todd Phillips'
long-awaited Joker movie, a new challenger

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:09.530
has entered the arena in hopes of becoming
the new Best Joker Actor Ever.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.530
His name?

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:11.669
Joaquin Phoenix.

00:00:11.669 --> 00:00:12.669
His game?

00:00:12.669 --> 00:00:16.010
Well, doing his job and delivering the chilling
kind of performance he knows is required of

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:19.760
him, but possibly also dethroning the late
Heath Ledger in the process.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.740
Since the announcement of Joker, fans have
pit Phoenix and Ledger against one another,

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:29.070
placing bets on whether or not the newcomer
could shock and scare audiences as the failed-comedian-turned-crazed-killer

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:33.410
Arthur Fleck as much as Ledger did through
his turn in Christopher Nolan's The Dark Knight.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:37.150
The debate over Phoenix and Ledger as the
Joker began months ago, but with the world

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:41.700
finally able to see Phoenix strut his stuff
in clown makeup and a tattered suit, the fight

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:42.750
is no longer theoretical.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:47.940
So, now that Joker has landed in theaters,
who played the character better: Joaquin Phoenix

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:48.940
or Heath Ledger?

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:52.920
Plenty of people were totally floored by the
work Phoenix did in Joker, so much so that

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.790
they now consider him better in the role than
the late Ledger.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:58.810
Some even think Phoenix is the best Joker
actor point blank.

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:01.309
"Are you having any negative thoughts?"

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:07.409
"All I have are negative thoughts."

00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:08.409
One Twitter user wrote:

00:01:08.409 --> 00:01:12.500
"With all due respect to previous Jokers and
to the great Heath Ledger, Joaquin Phoenix

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.740
is the best Joker.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.179
He has everything it needs.

00:01:15.179 --> 00:01:19.380
We finally have a proper actor playing the
character in a very unfamiliar new shape.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.139
If Ledger's a straight flush, Phoenix's a
full deck."

00:01:22.139 --> 00:01:23.429
Another fan tweeted:

00:01:23.429 --> 00:01:27.320
"I thought it would take a long time before
someone delivers Joker better than Heath Ledger.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.180
As it turned out it only took 11 years and
a certain Joaquin Phoenix."

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:35.119
This fan continued to gush over Phoenix's
performance in another tweet, writing,

00:01:35.119 --> 00:01:39.700
"Joaquin Phoenix should get an Oscar, a golden
globe, an Olympic gold medal, a Nobel prize,

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:44.789
a ballon d'or, Knighthood, a champions league
winner medal and a presidential medal of freedom

00:01:44.789 --> 00:01:46.429
for his performance as the joker."

00:01:46.429 --> 00:01:51.329
Bollywood news &amp; gossip site KoiMoi.com aimed
to settle the debate once and for all.

00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:52.820
Their breathless verdict?

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.329
Phoenix wins, hands down:

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:58.099
"Phoenix's portrayal of Arthur Fleck is going
to be remembered for a lifetime.

00:01:58.099 --> 00:02:02.649
His portrayal is so powerful that after the
film was over I was so sucked into his world

00:02:02.649 --> 00:02:04.669
that I felt like I needed a good sleep.

00:02:04.669 --> 00:02:08.539
Phoenix's performance makes you feel sorry
for being a part of this society and hence

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:13.829
I say…Joaquin Phoenix'[s] Joker makes Heath
Ledger's Joker even more badass than he was!"

00:02:13.829 --> 00:02:17.909
But, alas, there can be no Phoenix-Joker-lovers
without Phoenix-Joker-detractors.

00:02:17.909 --> 00:02:22.159
In the outlet's comprehensive ranking of every
Joker, Polygon placed Ledger several spots

00:02:22.159 --> 00:02:26.360
higher than Phoenix, with Ledger coming in
second place behind Mark Hamill, who voiced

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:30.670
the Ace of Knaves on Batman: The Animated
Series, and Phoenix coming in fifth just ahead

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.830
of Suicide Squad actor Jared Leto.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:36.590
Polygon's Susana Polo said of Phoenix's turn
as the iconic comic villain:

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:41.069
"His Arthur Fleck is impossible to look away
from, even when you desperately want to.

00:02:41.069 --> 00:02:46.140
Phoenix sways, grimaces, shuffles, and delivers
terrible, involuntary paroxysms of laughter

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.410
even as he openly weeps.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.700
He just does it in service of a character
who isn't particularly Joker-like, other than

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:53.329
in the most superficial ways."

00:02:53.329 --> 00:02:57.010
Comparatively, Polygon's Patrick Willems wrote
that Ledger delivered a performance, quote,

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:01.150
"so good it's worth forgiving it for all the
terrible Halloween costumes and cosplays it

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:02.150
inspired."

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.879
"Wanna see a magic trick?

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:10.880
I'm gonna make a pencil... disappear."

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.230
On a different note, Jesse Hassenger of The
Week wrote that Phoenix's version of the Joker

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:19.770
falls short of not only the magnitude of Ledger's
iteration, but also that of the power of every

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.629
Joker actor who preceded him.

00:03:21.629 --> 00:03:22.629
Hassenger wrote:

00:03:22.629 --> 00:03:25.349
"Even an actor as gifted as Joaquin Phoenix
struggles with this.

00:03:25.349 --> 00:03:29.719
Todd Phillips' new Joker is a vastly more
focused, disciplined undertaking than something

00:03:29.719 --> 00:03:34.049
like Suicide Squad, with a committed and often
mesmerizing performance from Phoenix.

00:03:34.049 --> 00:03:38.680
Yet it still often feels more like a composite
of influences than a real original...This

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.670
is all very well-performed by Phoenix; it's
also more indebted to Jokers past than the

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:43.670
movie seems to understand.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:48.510
The movie wants desperately to make the Joker
feel real and resonant, and Phoenix does his

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:49.510
best.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:53.209
But ultimately, this may mark another transition
for the Joker: a turning point from prestige

00:03:53.209 --> 00:03:54.480
role to party trick."

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:58.829
With so many different versions of the Joker
in existence, no singular take on the iconic

00:03:58.829 --> 00:04:01.139
villain can be universally heralded as the
best.

00:04:01.139 --> 00:04:04.499
There really is no "best" Joker actor, it's
entirely subjective.

00:04:04.499 --> 00:04:08.909
That said, being able to find even a little
bit of greatness in each of them just shows

00:04:08.909 --> 00:04:12.120
how iconic the Clown Prince of Crime really
is.

